event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":270,"item_id":"msg_032d8c994a0816a5016adb3665a9d08191bc50e6e7401088d0","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"Submitted candidate 1, based on `prior-candidate.json`, with the bookkeeping repair: S004 now lists its use of F001. The structural check passed; it is not mathematical acceptance.\n\nThe disputed coefficient objection is incorrect. From the stated formula,\n\\[\nX_r e_t=\\binom{\\lambda-t+r}{r}e_{t-r},\n\\]\nsetting \\(t=\\lambda\\) and \\(r=\\lambda-i\\) gives coefficient \\(\\binom{\\lambda-i}{\\lambda-i}=1\\), not \\(\\binom{2(\\lambda-i)}{\\lambda-i}\\). The other identity in S002 has coefficient \\(\\binom{j+(\\lambda-j)}{\\lambda-j}=\\binom{\\lambda}{j}\\), a unit in \\(\\mathbb Z_{(p)}\\) since \\(\\lambda<p\\). Thus the cited \\(\\lambda=2,p=3\\) objection does not apply.\n\nThe submitted proof retains the expanded basis argument and the corrected reduced-basis identification. I could not add the requested explicit index-by-index expansion to the artifact: after the first submission the stage was marked complete, and the attempted same-candidate edit was rejected. The submitted S002 already states the relevant identities, but it does not include that extra expansion.","logprobs":[]}

